==English==
{{was wotd|2019|June|8}}

===Etymology===
[[File:Polynya off the Antarctic Coast - NASA Earth Observatory.jpg|thumb|An image of a polynya ''(right, labelled)'' off the coast of [[Antarctica]] near [[Ross Island]], taken on 16 November 2011 by the US {{w|National Aeronautics and Space Administration}}’s {{w|Moderate Resolution Imaging Spectroradiometer}} (MODIS) on the [[satellite]] [[w:Aqua (satellite)|Aqua]]]]

Borrowed from {{bor|en|ru|полынья́||polynya}}<ref>{{R:Lexico}}</ref> in the 1850s, from {{der|en|zle-mru|полыньѧ}} (att. in 1639), from {{m|zle-mru|полыи||open from above, [[uncovered]]; hollow}}, whence also {{cog|ru|полый||hollow}}, from {{der|en|orv|полъ||uncovered}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*pleh₂-||flat}}. The rare plural form ''polynyi'' is borrowed from {{bor|en|ru|полыньи́}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|part of speech=n|code=147267|date=September 2006}}</ref>

